::ingredients

(water) 7.5 cups / 1.75 litres
(split peas, dried green) 1.5 cups / 300g
(pork belly choice) = (pork belly, Dutch speklapjes) 3.5oz / 100g -OR- (bacon, thick) 3.5oz / 100g
(pork chop) 1
(bouillon cube, vegetable or pork or chicken) 1
(celery) 2 ribs
(carrot, peeled and sliced) 2-3
(potato, large, peeled and cubed) 1
(onion, small, chopped) 1
(leek, small, sliced) 1
(celeriac, cubed) 1 cup
(rookworst, smoked, chopped) 1lb
(salt) to taste
(pepper) to taste
(celery leaves, chopped) for garnish

::equipment

(pot)
(immersion blender, optional)

::instructions

(water) + (split peas) + (pork belly choice) + (pork chop) + (bouillon cube) <bring to boil>
    <simmer, covered, 45m, stir and skim>
(pork chop) <remove> <debone> <slice, thinly> <set aside>
(celery) + (carrot) + (potato) + (onion) + (leek) + (celeriac) <add, to soup>
{soup} <bring to boil> <simmer, uncovered, 30m>
(rookworst) <add, for final 15m of simmering>
(pork belly choice) + (rookworst) <remove, when vegetables tender> <slice, thinly> <set aside>
Optional [
    {soup} <blend, immersion blender>
]
{soup} + (salt) + (pepper) <season>
    + (pork chop) + (pork belly choice) + (rookworst) all except some reserved for garnish <combine>
<serve, warm bowls, garnish with reserved sausage and celery leaves>

::story

Erwtensoep, also called snert, is the Dutch version of pea soup.
Slices of rookworst (smoked sausage) are added before serving. The soup, which is traditionally eaten during the winter, is emblematic of Dutch cuisine.
It is customarily served with Frisian rye bread (roggebrood) and bacon, cheese or butter.
Pancakes are sometimes served with pea soup; this dish is called snert met struif, struif referring to the pancakes.

